                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "246209a6-4589-3704-b7ac-7aacd4912bee",
                                        "entry_id": "518a2362-a402-3e1c-8bd1-c14b29e10c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An individual step, or stage, in any process or scale of values."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2defd38-00ea-3ad5-87a9-15a15e50ab0c",
                                        "entry_id": "518a2362-a402-3e1c-8bd1-c14b29e10c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stage of rank or privilege; social standing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d98cd23-84f5-42b0-9ce2-34eaa7a51bda",
                                                "sense_id": "a2defd38-00ea-3ad5-87a9-15a15e50ab0c",
                                                "text": "And they axed hym ſayinge: Maſter / we knowe that thou ſayest / and teacheſt ryght / nether conſidereſt thou eny mãnes degre / but teacheſt the waye of god truely."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eeecb781-b17a-4380-9c4f-7bd3a45a6261",
                                                "sense_id": "a2defd38-00ea-3ad5-87a9-15a15e50ab0c",
                                                "text": "But when Adam delued, and Eue ſpan,\nVVho was then a Gentleman.\nBrethren, brethren, it were better to haue this communitie,\nThen to haue this difference in degrees:\nThe landlord his rent, the lawyer his fees.\nSo quickly the poore mans ſubſtance is ſpent […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41536488-1afd-3d7b-86c6-b3eccc591b09",
                                        "entry_id": "518a2362-a402-3e1c-8bd1-c14b29e10c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ‘step’ in genealogical descent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1d7ee1d-57fd-4ed0-9099-a50f4366db5f",
                                                "sense_id": "41536488-1afd-3d7b-86c6-b3eccc591b09",
                                                "text": "Louis created the École militaire in Paris in 1751, in which 500 scholarships were designated for noblemen able to prove four degrees of noble status."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b32ea2b7-7878-35d2-b2a6-2d9045d6af37",
                                        "entry_id": "518a2362-a402-3e1c-8bd1-c14b29e10c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One's relative state or experience; way, manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1d92a30-2bfb-4e36-b327-d42ade61c48a",
                                                "sense_id": "b32ea2b7-7878-35d2-b2a6-2d9045d6af37",
                                                "text": "If they but knew it, almost all men in their degree, some time or other, cherish very nearly the same feelings towards the ocean with me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c0db822-2375-3f6d-be85-a46653619941",
                                        "entry_id": "518a2362-a402-3e1c-8bd1-c14b29e10c2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The amount that an entity possesses a certain property; relative intensity, extent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a36d7aef-6516-4b50-ad1e-d8dcea0010a4",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0db822-2375-3f6d-be85-a46653619941",
                                                "text": "To what degree do the two accounts of the accident concur?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2888736-813a-4499-b70c-3a7763ffbc0e",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0db822-2375-3f6d-be85-a46653619941",
                                                "text": "In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts, […], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "500dd183-9799-4e1a-aa2d-6cbf0358339d",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0db822-2375-3f6d-be85-a46653619941",
                                                "text": "Then there are the sums that Abramovich would be permitted to invest within the parameters of the profit and sustainability rules – £105m over a rolling three-year period. That, plainly, has stopped and so, to repeat, it is imperative that the transfer of ownership happens with a degree of speed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
